  "mechanismSummary": "2-Methylcyclohexanone can form two enolates. LDA at −78 °C removes a proton from the less hindered CH₂ side fastest, and under these conditions the enolates do not interconvert: this kinetic enolate is the main one, and iodomethane alkylates it to 2,6-dimethylcyclohexanone. The more substituted, thermodynamic enolate (giving 2,2-dimethylcyclohexanone) is drawn as the minor route; it dominates only when the enolates can equilibrate.",
